# Tailwind CSS: Inline-First Approach

## Primary Rule

Always use inline Tailwind classes directly in JSX/TSX and PHP files. Keep components self-contained with all styles inline.

## Examples

```jsx
// ✅ GOOD - Inline Tailwind with arbitrary values
<div className="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-[0_4px_6px_-1px_rgba(0,0,0,0.05)] hover:shadow-[0_20px_25px_-5px_rgba(0,0,0,0.1)] hover:-translate-y-1 transition-all duration-300">

// ✅ GOOD - Complex hover effects inline
<div className="absolute top-1/2 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 hover:scale-110 hover:rotate-12 transition-all duration-300 [box-shadow:0_20px_40px_-10px_rgba(217,119,6,0.5)]">

// ❌ BAD - Creating custom classes in main.css
// main.css: .my-card { @apply bg-white rounded-2xl; box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
// component: <div className="my-card">
```

## When main.css IS Allowed

Only add to `app/public/wp-content/themes/nera-competitions-standard/src/main.css` when:

1. **@keyframes animations** - Complex animations not possible with Tailwind
2. **Browser-specific fixes** - Vendor prefixes like -webkit-scrollbar
3. **Global utilities** - Used across 10+ files (e.g., .line-clamp-2)
4. **Print styles** - @media print rules
5. **Unavailable CSS features** - Custom scrollbar styling, CSS Grid named areas

## Migration Pattern

When refactoring existing CSS:
1. Read all properties from the custom class in main.css
2. Convert each property to Tailwind inline classes
3. Use arbitrary values `[property:value]` for custom values
4. Delete the custom class from main.css
5. Update component to use only inline classes

## Arbitrary Values Syntax

Use Tailwind's arbitrary value syntax for custom values:
- Shadows: `shadow-[0_4px_6px_-1px_rgba(0,0,0,0.05)]`
- Colors: `bg-[#f5f5f5]`
- Spacing: `p-[17px]`
- Any property: `[box-shadow:0_20px_40px_-10px_rgba(217,119,6,0.5)]`
